      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Fleshling" hidden="false" id="2289-dded-ac9c-1317">
          <costs>
            <cost name="Auri" typeId="cost-auri" value="8"/>
          </costs>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="10" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="f288-c005-e2e6-90ef" includeChildSelections="false"/>
            <constraint type="max" value="30" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="ef4d-2c0f-4f08-924e" includeChildSelections="false"/>
          </constraints>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Auri" typeId="cost-auri" value="10"/>
      </costs>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Feral Horde" id="6273-eff0-eb60-1189" hidden="false">
          <description>This unit counts as having an Initiative characteristic of 3 for the purposes of making Cut Them Down reactions, and this unit attacks with advantage when making such a reaction.
In addition, this unit can never contest or claim objective markers, and it ignores the effects of attrition points. Lastly, victory points cannot be scored for any objectives by destroying this unit.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Blood Magic" id="6256-00f0-effd-19b5" hidden="false">
          <description>During the combat phase, a friendly *Kingdoms of Mikhaelhelde* *mystic* unit can channel their power through this unit. If it does so, it can invoke the power as if it were using Wild Magic, if any doubles are rolled, instead of gaining *unbound insanity*, D5 models from this unit are slain.
A unit with this ability can only be used to channel another unit&apos;s power once per turn.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Fleshwrought Abominations (10+)" id="a060-a880-6661-0905" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="50b6-7cf2-2776-06ae"/>
